cond attempt finished successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why v2.3.1 reached production after failing in staging, and investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I'll check whether the incident was created before trying again, to avoid paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01N5rp2odZwLmMqTHfrs9SeQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks everywhere, with an error rate of 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging before it went to production.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to that. It was healthy in production before, so it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt failed with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back is safe to repeat, so I ran it again and it finished in every region.\n- Current state: us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and it had gone through as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open). I didn't retry, so on-call was paged only once.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback and the halted first 